Build the menu as a dictionary with snack names as keys and prices as values.
Look up a price with square brackets, for example menu["popcorn"].
Add the two lookups together and store the result in a total variable.
An f-string like f"${total:.2f}" formats the price for the receipt line.
For the coupon, use if total > 5 to subtract 1.00, with an else branch for the other case.
